2026-10-07,algebra-vs-geometry cross-corpus atlas run (Atlas-2 pipeline),pass,,,,blind,,"Claim in router's words: mapping algebra and geometry would show a very narrow link between the two constellations, similarly to Atlas-2. Router declined granular precision; bar is qualitative ('very narrow link, similarly'). Quantitative bar (adjudicated-link share, genuine-merge count) to be fixed at run-design time, before the run executes, and noted here. Item 3; blind arm per coin flip; p_router pending. CORRECTION 2026-10-07 (router): he meant ANALYTICS (analytic number theory), not algebra — dictation slip. The algebra run proceeds as chartered: it tests the same structural prediction (two skies, narrow link), and the analytics-vs-geometry mapping is the natural follow-up."
2026-10-07,Atlas-4: AI research skies mapped with the Atlas pipeline,pass,0.775,0.7,,shown,,"Claim in router's words: whatever program was launched that resulted in AI in the first place was very similar to this (the narrow-links-between-skies structure). Operationalized: mapping AI's research skies (symbolic, connectionist, statistical ML, neuroscience) shows dense within-sky constellations, narrow between-sky links, breakthroughs on the narrow bridges — at Atlas-2/3-like density. p_ai_1=Muse=0.70 (shown arm per coin flip): three trenches show the pattern; the symbolic/connectionist split is historically documented as hostile-disjoint; discount for thin pilot trench and weak cross-vocabulary recall. p_router pending. p_router=0.775: router stated '75 to 80% chance that they were trying to map relations' — midpoint recorded for scoring, range preserved verbatim here."
